2026-06-29 WIP
- Removed legacy yesmenn:* light ID/resource compatibility from L?YM while keeping shared YesMenn creative tab integration.
- Fixed slider-drag GUI dim by removing extra black overlay.
- Tint invisible spotlight marker with configured color and render it fullbright.
- Switched panel active plane to emissive model and added NeoForge fullbright data to panel/tube emitters.
- VILC test: reconstruct screen position from gl_FragCoord and disable first-person additive bubble pass.
- GUI dim also redraws number fields at drag opacity.
- Reverted vanilla/no-shader additive blend test because it overbrightened the scene.
- Center number input values in the light GUI during normal rendering.
- Wire colored light panel active plane to the fullbright model.
- VILC binds a dummy complete 3D texture for uBlockGrid when voxel shadows are unavailable to avoid GL_INVALID_OPERATION program texture usage.
- VILC vanilla pass now uses RenderTarget viewWidth/viewHeight for viewport and texcoord normalization.
- Add tint index to colored light panel fullbright plane.
- VILC disables and restores GL scissor state around the fullscreen light pass to rule out clipped quadrant artifacts.
- VILC samples depth with the actual depth texture size while keeping screen coordinates normalized to the visible view to avoid stale render-target quadrant reads.
2026-06-29 WIP: Added big spotlight and invisible pointlight; renamed internal spotlight models/textures from colored_light_spotlight* to colored_spotlight*.
2026-06-29 WIP: Replaced invisible marker model with separate invisible spotlight and pointlight models.
2026-07-02 - VILC/L?YM vanilla quadrant debugging
- Status: Quadranten weiterhin sichtbar bei Iris Shaderpack OFF; Shaderpack ON blendet sie aus, aber Lichtpfad ist dort aktuell separat kaputt/nachrangig.
- Ausgeschlossen: Light resolve/compositeFramebuffer als alleinige Ursache. Direct composite von lightTexture statt resolvedLightTexture hat Quadranten nicht entfernt.
- Beobachtung: GL_INVALID_OPERATION "program texture usage" spammt weiter, daher Verdacht auf Feedback/invalid texture attachment during composite.
- Naechster Versuch: Vanilla composite ohne GL_DST_COLOR Destination-Blend. Scene-Farbe zuerst in separate Texture kopieren, dann Scene+Light in Shader berechnen und ohne Blend zurueck in Main-FBO schreiben.
2026-07-02 - Versuch: Vanilla composite ohne Destination-Blend
- Geaendert in VILC IrisVeilLightPass: Vanilla-Pfad kopiert die bestehende Scene zuerst in resolvedLightTexture.
- Danach schreibt der Composite-Shader Scene * (1 + Light) ohne GL_BLEND in das Main-FBO zurueck.
- Non-vanilla/Iris-Pfad bleibt auf altem Light-only Shader + GL_DST_COLOR Blend, damit dieser Test gezielt den Shaderpack-OFF/Vanilla-Pfad isoliert.
- Build: VILC compileJava + assemble erfolgreich; Jar nach L?YM run/mods kopiert.
- Testziel: Wenn Quadranten/GL_INVALID_OPERATION verschwinden, war der Vanilla-Destination-Blend/Main-FBO-Composite die Ursache. Wenn nicht, liegt der Fehler frueher im LightTexture-Inhalt oder in externer FBO/Texture-State-Kopplung.
2026-07-02 - Testfeedback Scene-copy Composite
- Screenshot 13:31 zeigt Fortschritt: Scene/Farben anderer Lights kommen durch die Quadranten durch, der Effekt ist nicht mehr komplett als hartes Overlay davor.
- Schluss: Composite/Main-FBO-Feedback war mindestens Teil des Problems, aber die Quadranten sind noch im Light-Anteil vorhanden.
- Naechster Fokus: LightTexture-Erzeugung selbst pruefen, besonders Depth-Sampling/Depth-UV/Viewport und ob bei vanilla der falsche Depth-Buffer bzw. falsche Depth-Aufloesung rekonstruiert wird.
2026-11-02 - Veil 4.5.2 + cleanup/perf pass
- Updated Veil dependency to 4.5.2 (modrinth version IpGnlNgK), minimum versionRange [4.5.2,).
- Magenta checkerboard/hand with Iris was Veil's own light pass sampling a missing albedo buffer (Veil disables dynamic buffers whenever Iris is loaded); fixed in VILC (MixinVeilNativeLightPass). Without Iris L?YM! uses plain Veil unchanged.
- Light manager: only lights on moving Sable sublevels update per frame; static lights update on client tick.
- Disabled (redstone-off) lights are freed from Veil instead of kept at brightness 0.
- VILC area-shape bridge, VILC shader-pass check and block-entity client hooks resolve their method handles once instead of reflecting on every call; mod-loaded checks are cached.
- Block tint chunk rebuild only runs when the color actually changes, not on every block-entity update.
- Light GUI sends server updates throttled to 10/s (always flushed on close) instead of 2 packets per slider step.
- Server rejects light edits from players who may not build there (adventure mode, spawn protection, unloaded chunk).
- Spawn protection index drops empty chunk entries; removed unused markDirty stubs.
- L?YM! color settings (exposure/strength/saturation/neutral) now always apply to its lamps, also with VILC installed (previously ignored whenever VILC was loaded). Defaults are neutral.
- Config screens: L?YM! alone -> L?YM! screen; VILC alone -> VILC screen; both -> combined "Lights? YesMenn! + VILC" screen from every entry point (both mod-list entries and VILC's O key) via ConfigScreenBridge.registerCombinedScreen. Removed unused openFromVilc.
- License changed to CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (LICENSE file with summary + full legal code, bundled into the jar as META-INF/LICENSE; mod_license=CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0).
- License switched from CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 to the YesMenn Custom License 1.0 (same LICENSE as VILC; bundled as META-INF/LICENSE).
- v1.1.1: spotlights now create real Veil SpotLightData (cone = Veil size, softness converted to Veil's soft-edge angle; focus and lens size via VILC). Panels stay area lights. Optional VILC dependency [1.5.2,) because older VILC cannot render spot lights.
